WEBVTT

1
00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.150
Good morning,
Mr. Sullivan.

2
00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:56.443
I have a meeting
in a few minutes

3
00:03:56.527 --> 00:03:59.029
with some very jittery
stockholders, Mattson.

4
00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:01.907
I hope you have
good news for me.

5
00:04:01.991 --> 00:04:04.993
Yes, sir. I do, sir.

6
00:04:05.161 --> 00:04:06.828
Every supermarket
tabloid in the country

7
00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:09.957
is running headlines about Andy
Barclay and his killer Good Guy doll.

8
00:04:10.041 --> 00:04:12.167
What about his mother and the
police that were on the case?

9
00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:13.835
The police were smart.
They denied everything,

10
00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.295
which is fine because
now they can't hurt us.

11
00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:16.463
But the mother's
a different matter.

12
00:04:16.547 --> 00:04:18.465
She backed up her
boy's story in court,

13
00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:21.009
so now she's under
psychiatric observation.

14
00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:22.427
Jesus.
Where's the boy now?

15
00:04:22.512 --> 00:04:26.265
Midtown Children's Crisis
Center. Foster custody is pending.

16
00:04:26.849 --> 00:04:30.477
My stomach hurts, Mattson. Is
this what you call good news?

17
00:04:30.561 --> 00:04:32.646
Yes... No.
I'm getting to that, sir.

18
00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:34.606
Our biggest problem has
been the rumors. A lot...

19
00:04:34.691 --> 00:04:36.483
Good morning,
Mr. Sullivan.

20
00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:39.444
A lot of people are saying that
some joker here at the company

21
00:04:39.529 --> 00:04:42.781
must have tampered with the
doll's voice cassette, you know?

22
00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:46.076
"Hi. I'm Chucky.
I'm the Lakeshore Strangler.

23
00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:49.871
"And now I'm gonna
kill you. " Something like...

24
00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:52.040
Well, something
like that.

25
00:04:52.333 --> 00:04:54.376
But the
good news, Mr. Sullivan,

26
00:04:54.544 --> 00:04:56.628
is that now
we've got the doll.

27
00:05:02.844 --> 00:05:04.094
We've rebuilt it
from head to toe.

28
00:05:04.178 --> 00:05:05.637
A lot of it was
burned to a crisp,

29
00:05:05.722 --> 00:05:07.889
but everything checks out, the
voice cassettes, the servomechanisms.

30
00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:09.391
We've found
absolutely nothing.

31
00:05:09.559 --> 00:05:10.976
This is
a quality control report.

32
00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:13.270
I'm sure it will make
the stockholders very happy.

33
00:05:13.396 --> 00:05:15.022
I want to see
the doll for myself.

34
00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:16.523
Absolutely.

35
00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:20.277
Gentlemen, Mr.
Sullivan's here. We ready?

36
00:05:20.403 --> 00:05:23.030
Well, give us a minute. We're
not used to making them manually.

37
00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:51.141
What's wrong? I don't know. It's stuck.

38
00:05:51.267 --> 00:05:52.934
Just...

39
00:05:53.102 --> 00:05:55.187
They'll have
this worked out.

40
00:06:05.448 --> 00:06:06.865
My God!

41
00:06:06.991 --> 00:06:08.450
Oh, Jesus!

42
00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:24.966
Andy, you still
dreaming about Chucky?

43
00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:27.594
Sometimes.

44
00:06:29.639 --> 00:06:31.223
You want to talk about it? No.

45
00:06:31.307 --> 00:06:34.643
Come on, Andy.
Remember what I told you?

46
00:06:35.353 --> 00:06:36.561
Talking helps make

47
00:06:36.646 --> 00:06:38.605
the nightmares go away.
The nightmares go away.

48
00:06:42.276 --> 00:06:46.029
Well, Chucky was
trying to take over my soul.

49
00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:47.322
Why?

50
00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:51.034
He was this bad man who
got inside my Good Guy doll,

51
00:06:51.119 --> 00:06:52.828
so he wouldn't
have to go to hell.

52
00:06:53.287 --> 00:06:55.872
But then he wanted
to get inside me.

53
00:06:56.249 --> 00:06:57.290
Why, Andy?

54
00:06:58.543 --> 00:07:02.796
'Cause if he stayed inside the doll
too long, he'd be trapped in there.

55
00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:06.508
He needed me 'cause I was the
first person he told his secret to.

56
00:07:08.386 --> 00:07:09.386
What secret?

57
00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.973
That his real name
was Charles Lee Ray.

58
00:07:14.308 --> 00:07:17.185
Boy, that's a scary dream.

59
00:07:18.354 --> 00:07:20.188
It was.

60
00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:24.693
Dreams can't hurt you.

61
00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:27.863
Dreams aren't real.

62
00:07:28.197 --> 00:07:30.031
Right?
Right.

63
00:07:30.533 --> 00:07:31.700
In here?

64
00:07:31.826 --> 00:07:32.951
In there.

65
00:07:34.287 --> 00:07:36.204
Let's hurry up.

66
00:07:40.126 --> 00:07:42.794
Mattson, I don't care what
it takes. Put a lid on this.

67
00:07:42.879 --> 00:07:44.629
Yes, sir. That's not a
problem. I'll take care of this.

68
00:07:44.714 --> 00:07:46.214
Listen to me.

69
00:07:46.466 --> 00:07:49.885
You smother this or you're out
of here in 24 hours. You got that?

70
00:07:50.011 --> 00:07:51.052
Yes, sir.

71
00:07:51.137 --> 00:07:55.765
Now, if you will excuse me, I've
got a meeting I've got to get to.

72
00:07:55.892 --> 00:07:58.101
As far as the stockholders
and I are concerned,

73
00:07:58.186 --> 00:07:59.895
this matter is finished.

74
00:07:59.979 --> 00:08:01.229
Yes, sir.

75
00:08:01.898 --> 00:08:03.148
What do you want me
to do with the doll?

76
00:08:04.734 --> 00:08:07.110
Stick it up your ass.

77
00:08:09.739 --> 00:08:12.824
Naturally, he was badly
traumatized by the murders,

78
00:08:12.909 --> 00:08:16.244
but they bounce back
pretty fast at that age.

79
00:08:16.454 --> 00:08:17.746
Poor kid.

80
00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:22.918
What Andy needs now is a normal
family environment, a fresh start

81
00:08:23.002 --> 00:08:25.253
and a chance to
forget the past.

82
00:08:25.796 --> 00:08:28.340
Since you two have done
so well with so many kids,

83
00:08:28.424 --> 00:08:31.885
we were hoping you might foster
him until his mother recovers.

84
00:08:31.969 --> 00:08:34.304
There's always room for one more. Mmm.

85
00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.097
What's that
supposed to mean?

86
00:08:38.559 --> 00:08:40.393
Uh, well...

87
00:08:40.937 --> 00:08:45.440
He seems normal enough, but
how has all this affected him?

88
00:08:46.609 --> 00:08:48.318
Well, in order to
come to terms with

89
00:08:48.444 --> 00:08:50.654
something he couldn't
possibly understand,

90
00:08:50.738 --> 00:08:53.949
he turned it all into
a kind of fairy tale.

91
00:08:55.368 --> 00:08:58.286
He insisted his doll
was responsible.

92
00:08:58.788 --> 00:09:02.791
He said it was possessed by
the soul of Charles Lee Ray.

93
00:09:02.959 --> 00:09:04.125
Who?

94
00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:05.877
The Lakeshore Strangler.

95
00:09:05.962 --> 00:09:12.425
He murdered a dozen people in this
series of ritual voodoo killings.

96
00:09:15.763 --> 00:09:19.516
Are we even qualified to
take care of a boy like this?

97
00:09:20.309 --> 00:09:22.269
Well, I understand
your concern, Mr. Simpson,

98
00:09:22.395 --> 00:09:24.980
but I'm sure you can see that
this is just a child's way

99
00:09:25.064 --> 00:09:28.024
of coping with
a difficult situation.

100
00:09:28.818 --> 00:09:30.402
Andy's fine now.

101
00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:33.363
He just wants to
get on with his life.

102
00:09:41.163 --> 00:09:43.957
So, Andy,
what do you like to eat?

103
00:09:44.083 --> 00:09:45.667
All kinds of things.

104
00:09:46.419 --> 00:09:49.212
Well, what's your very favorite
food in the whole wide world?

105
00:09:49.714 --> 00:09:51.006
Chocolate.

106
00:09:52.216 --> 00:09:53.800
Besides chocolate.

107
00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:59.055
Mmm... My mom used to fix me
eggs for breakfast. I like eggs.

108
00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:02.017
You got it. We should stop at the store.

109
00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:04.185
The one down here?
Yeah, the organic one.

110
00:10:05.855 --> 00:10:08.398
You're in luck, Andy.
Joanne's a terrific cook.

111
00:10:09.859 --> 00:10:12.527
You like sushi?
You know what I mean by...

112
00:10:12.653 --> 00:10:13.695
Phil, look out!

113
00:10:13.821 --> 00:10:14.863
Jesus Christ!

114
00:10:38.721 --> 00:10:40.555
Look out
for the car.

115
00:10:40.681 --> 00:10:42.599
Hey, wait up.

116
00:10:52.902 --> 00:10:54.986
Make yourself comfortable,
Andy.

117
00:10:55.071 --> 00:10:56.696
Thanks.

118
00:11:01.243 --> 00:11:03.912
Well, I have to get back
to the office this afternoon.

119
00:11:04.497 --> 00:11:07.666
I thought that
you'd done everything.

120
00:11:40.241 --> 00:11:41.366
Ah-ah-ah...

121
00:11:42.451 --> 00:11:45.370
First rule.
Don't touch the old stuff.

122
00:11:45.454 --> 00:11:46.621
Sorry.

123
00:11:46.789 --> 00:11:47.997
Well, that's okay.
No foul.

124
00:11:48.082 --> 00:11:50.667
It's just that we
collect this junk,

125
00:11:50.793 --> 00:11:53.461
and a lot of it's
kind of fragile.

126
00:11:53.671 --> 00:11:55.547
You like it?
Uh-huh.

127
00:11:55.631 --> 00:11:57.632
It's been in my family
for three generations.

128
00:11:57.717 --> 00:12:01.261
My grandmother gave it to my
mother, and my mother gave it to me.

129
00:12:01.345 --> 00:12:03.888
And who are you
gonna give it to?

130
00:12:05.766 --> 00:12:07.475
Why don't you take this
upstairs and explore?

131
00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:08.643
I'll be up there
in a minute.

132
00:12:08.811 --> 00:12:09.936
Okay.

133
00:12:17.278 --> 00:12:18.820
What do you think?

134
00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:23.074
I'll get used to him.

135
00:12:41.802 --> 00:12:44.554
Jesus. Did you
ever hear of knocking?

136
00:12:45.055 --> 00:12:47.015
Andy, did you find...

137
00:12:47.099 --> 00:12:50.018
What, are you crazy?
Give them to me.

138
00:12:50.352 --> 00:12:51.603
Come on, Joanne.

139
00:12:51.687 --> 00:12:53.521
Phil will shoot you
if he catches you again.

140
00:12:53.647 --> 00:12:56.858
Andy, this is Kyle.
She's staying with us, too.

141
00:12:57.568 --> 00:12:59.027
Charmed.

142
00:12:59.195 --> 00:13:00.653
Kyle, what is this?

143
00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:04.407
You've been here three weeks.
Why haven't you unpacked?

144
00:13:04.533 --> 00:13:08.369
What for? I've never
spent more than a month in any home.

145
00:13:09.497 --> 00:13:11.039
With that attitude,
I can see why.

146
00:13:11.123 --> 00:13:12.123
Come on.
Put these things away,

147
00:13:12.208 --> 00:13:13.500
and then would
you do me a favor

148
00:13:13.626 --> 00:13:14.918
and help me get
dinner started?

149
00:13:15.002 --> 00:13:17.170
Can't.
Got to work tonight.

150
00:13:17.797 --> 00:13:19.547
Kyle, that's
the third night in a row.

151
00:13:19.632 --> 00:13:22.884
I'd really like it if you'd spend
a little time with the family.

152
00:13:23.511 --> 00:13:26.721
I need the money. I'm gonna
be on my own next year.

153
00:13:26.806 --> 00:13:30.183
Yes, well, until then,
you're with us, okay?

154
00:13:32.728 --> 00:13:34.687
Come along, Andy.
Bye.

155
00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:37.106
I think you'll be
very happy here.

156
00:13:42.404 --> 00:13:44.948
This is your room,
right here.

157
00:13:53.791 --> 00:13:55.583
I made those curtains
just for you.

158
00:13:55.751 --> 00:13:57.585
I bet blue is
your favorite color.

159
00:13:57.711 --> 00:14:00.421
Take a look around.
I'll start to unpack.

160
00:14:03.926 --> 00:14:05.051
Wow!

161
00:14:06.929 --> 00:14:11.182
I thought you might like those.
Um... There's more in the closet.

162
00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:15.937
Before dinner, we'll
go explore the backyard.

163
00:14:16.146 --> 00:14:18.147
And, later,
I'll read you some stories.

164
00:14:18.774 --> 00:14:20.400
Would you like that?

165
00:14:20.609 --> 00:14:22.777
There are lots of kids your
age in the neighborhood, Andy.

166
00:14:22.903 --> 00:14:25.989
I'm sure you're going to make
all sorts of new friends.

167
00:14:30.494 --> 00:14:31.619
Hey, hey!

168
00:14:32.162 --> 00:14:34.873
Andy, rule number two,
no running in the house.

169
00:14:35.457 --> 00:14:38.418
It's only a doll. Andy,
are you listening to me?

170
00:14:38.544 --> 00:14:41.504
Oh, Andy, I'm so sorry. I
didn't realize that was in there.

171
00:14:41.589 --> 00:14:43.715
We've had so many kids here, it's
hard to keep track of everything.

172
00:14:43.799 --> 00:14:45.049
I'll get rid of it.

173
00:14:45.301 --> 00:14:48.219
Hi, I'm Tommy. And I'm
your friend till the end.

174
00:14:48.304 --> 00:14:52.015
Why don't we get settled in, and
then we'll have some dinner, okay?

175
00:15:04.486 --> 00:15:06.112
Shit.

176
00:15:53.577 --> 00:15:56.120
Hello, Gabriella.
Guess who?

177
00:15:57.539 --> 00:15:59.457
That's right.

178
00:16:00.334 --> 00:16:03.294
The vodka? The vodka. Of
course I remembered the vodka.

179
00:16:03.379 --> 00:16:06.089
Two-week anniversary. You
think I'd forget the vodka?

180
00:16:06.173 --> 00:16:08.549
I know what
that does to you.

181
00:16:08.884 --> 00:16:10.593
Okay, well, wait for me.

182
00:16:11.387 --> 00:16:13.221
On my way. Yeah.

183
00:16:14.598 --> 00:16:16.140
Shit.

184
00:16:53.178 --> 00:16:54.512
I want to play
Red Light.

185
00:16:54.596 --> 00:16:56.723
No, Sammy, I don't want
to play Red Light now.

186
00:16:56.807 --> 00:16:58.349
I want you to go back to
bed right now.

187
00:16:58.475 --> 00:17:00.018
But I'm scared.

188
00:17:00.477 --> 00:17:03.813
There's nothing to be
scared of. It's just a storm.

189
00:17:06.942 --> 00:17:08.443
Grace Poole.

190
00:17:08.819 --> 00:17:12.113
Yes, I'm trying to
reach Andy Barclay.

191
00:17:12.322 --> 00:17:14.866
Andy no longer lives here.
Who is this?

192
00:17:15.617 --> 00:17:17.994
This is his Uncle Charles.

193
00:17:20.122 --> 00:17:21.956
Sorry, cash only.

194
00:17:22.124 --> 00:17:25.293
But that's a gold card.
That's just as good as cash.

195
00:17:25.377 --> 00:17:28.671
Not here, it ain't. We
don't accept credit cards.

196
00:17:29.089 --> 00:17:31.257
I don't
carry cash, okay?

197
00:18:16.845 --> 00:18:18.179
Don't move!

198
00:18:18.305 --> 00:18:19.639
Jesus!

199
00:18:19.973 --> 00:18:23.392
God. Okay. Okay,
what do you want?

200
00:18:23.685 --> 00:18:26.854
No questions. Just drive. Okay, okay.

201
00:18:34.029 --> 00:18:35.822
Keep going.

202
00:18:50.796 --> 00:18:54.507
Now, park
this piece of shit.

203
00:19:02.641 --> 00:19:04.934
Put your arms
behind the seat.

204
00:19:05.018 --> 00:19:07.061
What?
Do it!

205
00:19:08.147 --> 00:19:12.191
Okay. Take it easy. Take it
easy. Please, don't shoot.

206
00:19:12.401 --> 00:19:16.237
Look, I don't carry cash.
I got a gold card.

207
00:19:16.321 --> 00:19:18.489
I'll give you anything you
want. Tell me what you want.

208
00:19:18.574 --> 00:19:21.200
Freeze, asshole.

209
00:19:22.744 --> 00:19:24.370
Take my... Take the car.

210
00:19:24.454 --> 00:19:27.456
And you can drop me off, but
just, please, leave me alone.

211
00:19:27.624 --> 00:19:29.041
Please.

212
00:19:29.209 --> 00:19:30.918
Bang. You're dead.

213
00:19:48.979 --> 00:19:52.106
No! No! No!

214
00:19:56.778 --> 00:20:00.323
No! No! No!

215
00:20:53.585 --> 00:20:56.212
"The woodcutter argued
for a long time with his wife,

216
00:20:56.296 --> 00:20:59.048
"but she was such a horrid,
frightening woman when she was angry,

217
00:20:59.174 --> 00:21:02.468
"that in the end he
agreed to her plan.

218
00:21:03.345 --> 00:21:05.471
"In the morning,
their stepmother called them.

219
00:21:05.555 --> 00:21:09.350
"'I think it would be nice if we all
went into the forest today,' she said.

220
00:21:09.434 --> 00:21:11.102
"Hansel and Gretel
did not reply,

221
00:21:11.186 --> 00:21:13.854
"but followed their parents
into the dark forest. "

222
00:21:13.939 --> 00:21:16.691
Where they all lived
happily ever after.

223
00:21:17.192 --> 00:21:19.110
No, they don't.
Well, they do for now.

224
00:21:19.194 --> 00:21:20.945
We'll finish it
tomorrow night.

225
00:21:22.656 --> 00:21:23.948
Don't go.

226
00:21:24.074 --> 00:21:25.408
What's the matter?

227
00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:28.035
I miss my mother.

228
00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:29.537
Oh, honey, I know you do.

229
00:21:30.414 --> 00:21:32.123
Will I ever
see her again?

230
00:21:32.249 --> 00:21:33.958
Of course you will.
I promise.

231
00:21:35.669 --> 00:21:39.505
Don't worry. I'll stay with
you as long as you want.

232
00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:45.386
My mother used to sing to me.
Will you sing to me?

233
00:22:19.171 --> 00:22:20.338
Shit.

234
00:22:20.422 --> 00:22:21.922
Hi. I'm Tommy.

235
00:22:22.424 --> 00:22:24.258
Shut up, you idiot.

236
00:22:24.718 --> 00:22:29.055
I like to be hugged. I like to
be hugged. I like to be hugged.

237
00:22:29.264 --> 00:22:30.348
I like to be hugged...

238
00:22:30.474 --> 00:22:31.599
Hug this.

239
00:22:31.808 --> 00:22:34.435
I like to be hugged. I
like to be hugged. I like...

240
00:22:36.438 --> 00:22:39.732
What was that? Nothing.
Now, go to sleep.

241
00:22:39.900 --> 00:22:42.485
Nobody's going to hurt you.

242
00:23:17.229 --> 00:23:19.522
Eat dirt, Tommy.

243
00:23:27.030 --> 00:23:30.658
Do either of you have
anything to say about this?

244
00:23:31.034 --> 00:23:32.952
I think we should
talk to a lawyer first.

245
00:23:33.036 --> 00:23:36.622
Kyle, that's not funny. That
statue was very important to me.

246
00:23:38.083 --> 00:23:41.043
I think one of you
owes Joanne an apology.

247
00:23:41.795 --> 00:23:42.837
I'm innocent.

248
00:23:44.464 --> 00:23:45.840
Andy?

249
00:23:45.924 --> 00:23:47.299
I didn't do it.

250
00:23:49.094 --> 00:23:52.680
All right.
You leave me no choice.

251
00:23:52.889 --> 00:23:55.391
Until somebody fesses up,
you're both grounded.

252
00:23:56.351 --> 00:23:58.060
But I have
a date tonight.

253
00:23:58.145 --> 00:23:59.186
Sorry.

254
00:24:01.857 --> 00:24:05.860
This is exactly how I wanted to
spend my day off. Thanks a lot.

255
00:24:06.027 --> 00:24:08.279
But I didn't break the statue. Really.

256
00:24:08.405 --> 00:24:11.323
Yeah.
Maybe it just fell?

257
00:24:12.868 --> 00:24:16.078
Hey. You want to hear me
say your name backwards?

258
00:24:17.456 --> 00:24:18.706
Kyle.

259
00:24:20.041 --> 00:24:21.792
Hold this.

260
00:24:28.717 --> 00:24:31.343
Jesus. Give me that.

261
00:24:32.053 --> 00:24:33.345
What the hell do you
think you're doing?

262
00:24:33.722 --> 00:24:34.847
I wanted to taste it.

263
00:24:35.474 --> 00:24:37.266
Get real. It tastes like shit, okay?

264
00:24:37.392 --> 00:24:39.226
These things are
very bad for you.

265
00:24:39.394 --> 00:24:40.978
Then why do you do it?

266
00:24:41.062 --> 00:24:44.899
Because grown-ups are allowed to
do things that are bad for them.

267
00:24:45.400 --> 00:24:46.650
You're not a grown-up.

268
00:24:48.653 --> 00:24:50.237
You're beginning to
get on my nerves, Andy.

269
00:24:50.947 --> 00:24:53.032
Now, why don't you
give me a hand over here?

270
00:24:57.913 --> 00:25:01.373
Mr. Simpson is kind
of grouchy, isn't he?

271
00:25:01.625 --> 00:25:03.209
He's not so bad.

272
00:25:03.293 --> 00:25:04.376
I've had fosters
that would shoot you

273
00:25:04.461 --> 00:25:05.836
for staring at
them cross-eyed.

274
00:25:06.254 --> 00:25:07.254
Really?

275
00:25:07.422 --> 00:25:08.422
Sure.

276
00:25:08.507 --> 00:25:10.925
They figure you're not theirs.
You're just passing through.

277
00:25:11.009 --> 00:25:12.843
The minute you screw up...

278
00:25:12.969 --> 00:25:14.595
Argh!
They let you have it.

279
00:25:22.270 --> 00:25:25.523
I got to tell you, I'm not
happy with this whole thing.

280
00:25:26.316 --> 00:25:27.608
Having second thoughts?

281
00:25:27.692 --> 00:25:31.779
Well, you have to admit, he's
a very troubled little boy,

282
00:25:31.947 --> 00:25:35.699
and he obviously has not come to
terms with this whole doll thing.

283
00:25:37.661 --> 00:25:40.871
Look, all I'm saying
is that he may need

284
00:25:40.956 --> 00:25:44.291
more attention
than we can give him.

285
00:25:45.377 --> 00:25:47.962
Phil, Andy's been
through hell.

286
00:25:48.338 --> 00:25:51.465
You have to give him some
time. He'll settle down.

287
00:25:51.800 --> 00:25:54.802
Besides, I like him.

288
00:26:12.362 --> 00:26:13.445
I hate you.

289
00:26:14.447 --> 00:26:18.409
Hi. I'm... Tommy, and I'm
your friend to the end.

290
00:26:18.493 --> 00:26:20.411
Hi-de-ho.

291
00:26:50.150 --> 00:26:51.650
Hi.

292
00:26:52.235 --> 00:26:54.194
Hi.
Hi.

293
00:27:09.294 --> 00:27:11.795
Kyle, do you miss
your mom and dad?

294
00:27:13.340 --> 00:27:15.841
You can't miss
someone you never knew.

295
00:27:15.925 --> 00:27:17.843
Where are they?

296
00:27:18.637 --> 00:27:20.512
I have no idea.

297
00:27:20.597 --> 00:27:22.681
My dad left
before I was born.

298
00:27:22.766 --> 00:27:25.601
My mom put me up for
adoption when I was three.

299
00:27:26.895 --> 00:27:28.896
Do you remember her?

300
00:27:31.274 --> 00:27:33.400
I made it a point
to forget.

301
00:27:33.568 --> 00:27:35.527
It's easier that way.

302
00:27:36.738 --> 00:27:39.740
Hey. Break time.

303
00:27:39.866 --> 00:27:41.825
Move over.

304
00:27:42.243 --> 00:27:43.369
Want a push?

305
00:27:43.453 --> 00:27:44.745
No, thank you.

306
00:27:45.121 --> 00:27:46.497
Come on. It's fun.

307
00:27:46.581 --> 00:27:49.249
Come on, Andy, please, I
just want to sit here, okay?

308
00:27:49.376 --> 00:27:51.126
Too late. There you go.

309
00:27:51.419 --> 00:27:54.546
Andy, come on.
Give me a break. Stop it.

310
00:27:54.631 --> 00:27:56.298
No.

311
00:27:58.093 --> 00:27:59.802
Andy, I'll kill you.

312
00:28:02.263 --> 00:28:04.098
Come on. Let me off.

313
00:28:04.933 --> 00:28:06.308
Andy.

314
00:28:07.560 --> 00:28:08.936
I'll get you.

315
00:28:09.688 --> 00:28:11.313
Come on, Andy, cut it out.
Dinner!

316
00:28:11.856 --> 00:28:13.524
Come and get it.
Whoa!

317
00:28:13.692 --> 00:28:14.692
Aah!

318
00:28:14.859 --> 00:28:17.569
Mayhem.
Come on. I'll race you.

319
00:28:18.279 --> 00:28:20.155
Not fair.
You got a head start.

320
00:28:20.240 --> 00:28:23.575
Excuses, excuses.
Don't forget your doll.

321
00:29:33.688 --> 00:29:35.939
For Kyle.
Think she'll like it?

322
00:29:36.024 --> 00:29:37.775
What do I know
about teenage girls?

323
00:29:37.859 --> 00:29:39.109
More than you did
three weeks ago.

324
00:29:39.235 --> 00:29:40.486
I'm not so sure.

325
00:29:40.570 --> 00:29:42.237
I was thinking we should
get something for Andy.

326
00:29:42.322 --> 00:29:43.614
Make him feel
more settled.

327
00:29:43.698 --> 00:29:44.740
Any ideas?

328
00:29:44.824 --> 00:29:46.200
Yeah. How about
a Valium?

329
00:29:55.877 --> 00:29:57.544
Surprise.

330
00:29:57.712 --> 00:30:01.048
Did you miss me, Andy?
I sure missed you.

331
00:30:01.966 --> 00:30:03.592
I told you.

332
00:30:03.676 --> 00:30:06.345
We were going to be
friends to the end.

333
00:30:06.596 --> 00:30:09.890
And now it's time to play.

334
00:30:10.725 --> 00:30:12.434
I got a new game, sport.

335
00:30:12.852 --> 00:30:17.147
It's called Hide the Soul.

336
00:30:17.273 --> 00:30:20.901
And guess what? You're it.

337
00:30:23.279 --> 00:30:26.114
Ade due damballa.

338
00:30:27.242 --> 00:30:29.827
Give me the power, I beg...

339
00:30:31.913 --> 00:30:33.247
This isn't over,
you little shit.

340
00:30:33.373 --> 00:30:36.166
I'm not gonna spend the rest
of my life as a plastic freak.

341
00:30:36.292 --> 00:30:39.169
Next time you're alone,
you're mine.

342
00:30:42.257 --> 00:30:44.299
Oh, my God.

343
00:30:47.387 --> 00:30:48.804
It's Chucky. Look out!

344
00:30:48.888 --> 00:30:50.097
Shut up. You'll wake Phil and Joanne.

345
00:30:50.181 --> 00:30:51.223
Kill him! Kill him!

346
00:30:51.307 --> 00:30:52.391
Andy, stop it,
will you?

347
00:30:53.768 --> 00:30:55.269
What the hell is this, now?

348
00:30:55.353 --> 00:30:59.356
It's Chucky. I told you he'd find
me. He tried to take over my soul.

349
00:30:59.440 --> 00:31:01.567
Andy, calm down.

350
00:31:01.734 --> 00:31:03.235
You didn't have
to wait up.

351
00:31:03.361 --> 00:31:06.196
Yeah? You know, Kyle,
I don't believe you.

352
00:31:06.281 --> 00:31:09.157
You actually tied this child
up, so he wouldn't tell on you.

353
00:31:09.284 --> 00:31:11.076
Is that it?
Come on, Phil.

354
00:31:11.160 --> 00:31:12.870
Chucky did it.
That's enough now.

355
00:31:12.954 --> 00:31:14.788
Chucky? I've had it.

356
00:31:16.541 --> 00:31:18.125
But you've got
to kill him.

357
00:31:18.251 --> 00:31:19.835
Andy!

358
00:31:21.296 --> 00:31:23.964
Please, listen to me.
I'm not lying.

359
00:31:24.048 --> 00:31:25.716
If you don't kill him,
he'll come get me.

360
00:31:25.800 --> 00:31:28.051
Andy, calm down.

361
00:31:28.386 --> 00:31:30.470
I'm going to
get rid of it.

362
00:31:34.893 --> 00:31:38.186
There, see? He's gone.
He can't bother you anymore.

363
00:31:49.157 --> 00:31:50.991
No.

364
00:31:51.576 --> 00:31:53.827
I'm turning human again?

365
00:31:54.329 --> 00:31:57.831
If I don't get out of this
body soon, I'm screwed.

366
00:32:01.794 --> 00:32:03.503
Come on, Andy.
We're late.

367
00:32:03.588 --> 00:32:06.590
Andy. Don't forget
your lunch.

368
00:32:06.674 --> 00:32:08.175
Egg salad.

369
00:32:09.886 --> 00:32:11.219
Mmm, yum!

370
00:32:21.689 --> 00:32:24.316
Now, whatever you do,
don't act nervous, okay?

371
00:32:24.400 --> 00:32:28.195
They'll smell a new kid a mile
off. Just act like you belong.

372
00:32:28.571 --> 00:32:29.655
What are you looking for?

373
00:32:29.781 --> 00:32:30.864
Nothing.

374
00:32:31.407 --> 00:32:33.992
Is it Chucky
coming to get you?

375
00:32:36.329 --> 00:32:39.122
Andy, how did you manage to tie
yourself up like that last night?

376
00:32:39.207 --> 00:32:40.540
I already told you.

377
00:32:40.667 --> 00:32:41.959
Get real.

378
00:32:42.961 --> 00:32:46.171
You're just like everybody else.
You don't believe me either.

379
00:32:47.632 --> 00:32:50.133
Kyle?
Hey, Adam. Hi.

380
00:32:50.385 --> 00:32:53.178
Why'd you have to leave so early
last night? You missed all the fun.

381
00:32:53.262 --> 00:32:55.222
Story of my life.

382
00:33:53.156 --> 00:33:56.366
Come on now.

383
00:33:56.451 --> 00:33:57.993
Where is it?

384
00:33:58.786 --> 00:34:00.829
Where is it?

385
00:34:03.291 --> 00:34:04.458
Ah-ha!

386
00:34:05.460 --> 00:34:10.297
"Pinocchio jumped for joy,
shouting, 'I'm alive! I'm alive!'

387
00:34:10.631 --> 00:34:13.091
"Then the talking cricket
said... " What'd he say?

388
00:34:13.176 --> 00:34:17.512
"'If you're very, very good,
and promise to tell no lies,

389
00:34:17.597 --> 00:34:20.307
"'then you will
become a real, live boy. '

390
00:34:20.433 --> 00:34:23.143
"Boys who are bent on
following their caprices

391
00:34:23.227 --> 00:34:27.522
"and will have their own way,
sooner or later repent. "

392
00:34:27.648 --> 00:34:29.691
Get lost, microchip.

393
00:34:29.776 --> 00:34:31.651
Am I boring you, Andy?

394
00:34:32.278 --> 00:34:33.236
No, Miss...

395
00:34:33.321 --> 00:34:34.863
Kettlewell.

396
00:34:34.989 --> 00:34:36.573
Kettlewell.

397
00:34:36.699 --> 00:34:39.743
I have precious little patience
for disruptive students.

398
00:34:40.620 --> 00:34:42.079
But he just whacked...

399
00:34:42.163 --> 00:34:44.498
Especially new students,
whose utmost concern

400
00:34:44.582 --> 00:34:46.750
should be getting
on my good side.

401
00:34:48.544 --> 00:34:51.838
I want those desks spick and
span before anyone leaves.

402
00:35:11.317 --> 00:35:13.944
Andy! You think
this is funny?

403
00:35:14.028 --> 00:35:15.779
I didn't do that.

404
00:35:16.948 --> 00:35:19.741
Go ahead, kids. Don't forget
the spelling test tomorrow.

405
00:35:19.826 --> 00:35:23.161
Not you. Come over here.
Sit down and get comfy.

406
00:35:23.246 --> 00:35:24.871
You're going to be
here for a while.

407
00:35:24.997 --> 00:35:26.706
But I didn't do it,
I swear.

408
00:35:26.791 --> 00:35:28.917
No? Then who did?

409
00:35:30.795 --> 00:35:32.838
Don't even think about it.

410
00:35:33.965 --> 00:35:37.509
No toys. Head down.

411
00:35:50.857 --> 00:35:52.899
Head down.

412
00:36:35.526 --> 00:36:37.027
Peekaboo!

413
00:36:37.612 --> 00:36:41.364
Please, let me
out of here, Andy.

414
00:36:41.449 --> 00:36:43.158
It's dark in here.

415
00:36:44.118 --> 00:36:48.038
I promise I won't
kill anyone else. Okay?

416
00:36:49.123 --> 00:36:50.790
Now,
open the goddamn door.

417
00:36:52.752 --> 00:36:54.544
Let me out,
you little dick.

418
00:36:55.504 --> 00:36:57.214
Let me the fuck out.

419
00:37:15.274 --> 00:37:19.861
Andy, I told you to stay in
your seat. Come out of there.

420
00:37:20.863 --> 00:37:23.281
Open this door right now.

421
00:37:29.080 --> 00:37:30.914
Andy,
come out this very second.

422
00:37:30.998 --> 00:37:33.208
Andy! Andy!

423
00:37:35.211 --> 00:37:37.170
Andy?

424
00:37:53.396 --> 00:37:54.896
Andy?

425
00:38:04.198 --> 00:38:06.574
Andy, this isn't funny.

426
00:38:35.563 --> 00:38:41.735
You've been very naughty,
Miss Kettlewell.

427
00:39:08.429 --> 00:39:10.180
Andy, what's this
all about?

428
00:39:10.264 --> 00:39:14.851
Chucky followed me to school. He
tried to get me again, so I ran home.

429
00:39:15.936 --> 00:39:17.687
Do you know what's
he talking about?

430
00:39:17.772 --> 00:39:18.897
His teacher called,

431
00:39:18.981 --> 00:39:21.858
said she was keeping him
after school for detention,

432
00:39:21.942 --> 00:39:24.861
said he wrote
an obscenity on his paper.

433
00:39:25.780 --> 00:39:27.113
Chucky did it.

434
00:39:29.116 --> 00:39:30.950
All right, Andy.
Come on.

435
00:39:31.202 --> 00:39:32.619
This is going to stop,

436
00:39:32.703 --> 00:39:34.662
'cause I will not allow this
foolishness in my house.

437
00:39:34.789 --> 00:39:36.706
Do you understand? Open
the door. Oh, Phil...

438
00:39:36.791 --> 00:39:38.792
Joanne, please.

439
00:39:42.546 --> 00:39:44.214
Open the door.

440
00:39:46.592 --> 00:39:48.134
Open it.

441
00:39:51.639 --> 00:39:52.931
Open it!

442
00:40:00.523 --> 00:40:02.941
Now, I want you to look down
there and tell me what you see.

443
00:40:05.986 --> 00:40:06.986
It's Chucky, but...

444
00:40:07.071 --> 00:40:10.323
His name is Tommy,

445
00:40:11.033 --> 00:40:13.868
and he's been there
since last night, hasn't he?

446
00:40:15.246 --> 00:40:16.871
Hasn't he?

447
00:40:21.919 --> 00:40:25.880
For crying out loud, Joanne, the
child needs professional help.

448
00:40:25.965 --> 00:40:27.507
Stop pretending
you're worried about Andy.

449
00:40:27.675 --> 00:40:29.259
You never wanted him
here in the first place.

450
00:40:29.343 --> 00:40:30.969
That's not true.

451
00:40:31.053 --> 00:40:33.388
So, what are you suggesting
we do? Send him back?

452
00:40:33.472 --> 00:40:35.432
You don't have to make
it sound so horrible.

453
00:40:35.516 --> 00:40:37.892
Do you have any idea how
traumatic that would be?

454
00:40:37.977 --> 00:40:42.147
Traum... For whom, Joanne,
for him or for you?

455
00:40:42.773 --> 00:40:46.192
Look, if that kid stays here,
he's gonna tear this family apart.

456
00:40:46.444 --> 00:40:48.987
Family? Is this
what you call a family?

457
00:40:49.071 --> 00:40:51.197
Families don't just
give up on their children.

458
00:40:51.282 --> 00:40:55.368
Joanne,
he's not our child.

459
00:41:03.085 --> 00:41:05.086
It's not the end
of the world.

460
00:41:06.380 --> 00:41:08.047
But they're going
to send me away.

461
00:41:15.014 --> 00:41:17.056
You'll be okay.

462
00:41:18.309 --> 00:41:20.185
Where will I go?

463
00:41:20.519 --> 00:41:22.020
Andy.

464
00:41:23.856 --> 00:41:26.608
I've lived with dozens
of different families,

465
00:41:28.027 --> 00:41:29.903
and they always
seem to send me away

466
00:41:30.070 --> 00:41:31.946
just when I'm
getting comfortable,

467
00:41:32.031 --> 00:41:33.990
but you know what?
What?

468
00:41:34.366 --> 00:41:38.077
Every time it happens,
it just makes me stronger,

469
00:41:38.370 --> 00:41:42.040
because it reminds me that the
only one I can count on is myself.

470
00:41:43.334 --> 00:41:45.376
Okay? And you have
to learn that now.

471
00:41:47.129 --> 00:41:49.047
I know it sounds tough,

472
00:41:49.632 --> 00:41:51.424
but you'll deal with it.

473
00:41:53.302 --> 00:41:55.094
It doesn't matter.

474
00:41:55.763 --> 00:41:58.765
Wherever I go,
Chucky will find me.

475
00:46:04.595 --> 00:46:07.513
...advances over the
declines by a seven to six margin...

476
00:46:10.434 --> 00:46:11.893
What's wrong?

477
00:46:12.186 --> 00:46:14.645
I thought I heard
something downstairs.

478
00:46:14.730 --> 00:46:16.189
It's one of
the children.

479
00:46:16.315 --> 00:46:18.316
That's what I'm afraid of.

480
00:46:23.197 --> 00:46:26.032
Why fight it, Andy? We're
going to be very close.

481
00:46:26.158 --> 00:46:30.036
In fact, we're going to
be fucking inseparable.

482
00:46:41.256 --> 00:46:42.548
What the hell's
going on down...

483
00:46:44.968 --> 00:46:46.552
Andy...

484
00:46:47.721 --> 00:46:48.805
Put down the knife.

485
00:46:48.889 --> 00:46:50.556
But I need it for...

486
00:46:51.600 --> 00:46:55.061
Just put the knife down,
and we'll talk about it.

487
00:47:05.155 --> 00:47:07.323
Everything is
going to be just fine.

488
00:47:24.967 --> 00:47:27.176
How's it hanging, Phil?

489
00:47:37.104 --> 00:47:40.273
No. Oh, God, Phil.

490
00:47:42.109 --> 00:47:43.985
I'll call an ambulance.

491
00:47:44.152 --> 00:47:45.278
Phil. Phil.

492
00:47:47.906 --> 00:47:49.949
Oh, God! No!

493
00:47:50.075 --> 00:47:51.576
Oh, God!

494
00:47:53.745 --> 00:47:54.787
Get away from me!

495
00:47:58.458 --> 00:47:59.625
Oh, God!

496
00:48:08.135 --> 00:48:10.761
No, we didn't
hear anything. Nothing.

497
00:48:37.831 --> 00:48:40.249
I should have
listened to him.

498
00:48:40.500 --> 00:48:43.210
He'd be here now if only
I'd listened to him.

499
00:48:48.008 --> 00:48:50.009
It's not your fault.

500
00:48:56.767 --> 00:48:58.768
I'll take care of this.

501
00:49:09.738 --> 00:49:12.615
Andy, you'll be fine now.

502
00:49:12.699 --> 00:49:15.201
You come stay at the center
with us for a few days

503
00:49:15.369 --> 00:49:17.745
until we can find
you a new family.

504
00:49:18.705 --> 00:49:21.540
We've placed Kyle with
a number of families.

505
00:49:22.042 --> 00:49:23.751
Things always seem
to work out okay.

506
00:49:24.753 --> 00:49:26.253
Don't they?

507
00:49:26.546 --> 00:49:28.130
Yeah.

508
00:49:31.510 --> 00:49:33.469
There's your stuff.

509
00:49:36.139 --> 00:49:38.516
Come on, Andy.
Let's go.

510
00:49:40.185 --> 00:49:43.688
He's still in the cellar, Kyle.
Don't let him get you, too.

511
00:49:43.814 --> 00:49:45.231
Andy?

512
00:49:59.371 --> 00:50:01.580
We'll be out of your way
in just a minute here.

513
00:50:01.748 --> 00:50:04.667
Did anyone, besides the boy,
witness the accident?

514
00:50:06.211 --> 00:50:07.920
No.
Okay.

515
00:50:08.005 --> 00:50:09.672
Let's go.

516
00:52:22.973 --> 00:52:24.890
Joanne!

517
00:52:25.016 --> 00:52:26.892
Joanne!

518
00:54:20.215 --> 00:54:21.507
Joanne?

519
00:54:35.522 --> 00:54:37.189
Joanne!

520
00:55:45.425 --> 00:55:47.885
Bitch. You hurt me.

521
00:55:53.808 --> 00:55:55.851
How much further
till we get to the kid?

522
00:55:55.935 --> 00:55:57.102
A ways.

523
00:55:57.270 --> 00:55:58.479
Step on it.

524
00:55:58.772 --> 00:56:00.105
What's the rush?

525
00:56:00.190 --> 00:56:04.276
If I don't get out of this body
soon, I'll be trapped in here.

526
00:56:05.445 --> 00:56:07.279
What are you looking at?

527
00:56:17.499 --> 00:56:18.665
Floor it.

528
00:56:18.750 --> 00:56:21.126
Get real.
This is a station wagon.

529
00:56:21.461 --> 00:56:23.587
Shit!

530
00:56:23.838 --> 00:56:25.506
Pull over.

531
00:56:37.602 --> 00:56:39.520
Behave yourself.

532
00:56:39.687 --> 00:56:42.064
I'll kill you
if I have to.

533
00:56:44.317 --> 00:56:46.777
Okay, honey,
let's see your license.

534
00:56:51.282 --> 00:56:54.743
You were clocking 60 in a 45.
What's your hurry?

535
00:56:56.121 --> 00:56:57.329
I have a date.

536
00:56:58.081 --> 00:56:59.998
You're going to have
to do better than that.

537
00:57:01.835 --> 00:57:03.168
That's one of those
Good Guys, isn't it?

538
00:57:04.838 --> 00:57:06.130
Yes, it is.

539
00:57:06.339 --> 00:57:08.424
I love these things.
What's your name, buddy?

540
00:57:10.844 --> 00:57:12.428
Chucky.

541
00:57:12.804 --> 00:57:14.221
That's incredible.

542
00:57:15.432 --> 00:57:16.515
I'll say.

543
00:57:17.767 --> 00:57:19.351
What the hell's that?

544
00:57:25.483 --> 00:57:27.359
You've seen dolls that pee?

545
00:57:27.944 --> 00:57:29.862
This one bleeds.

546
00:57:34.409 --> 00:57:35.617
Okay, look,

547
00:57:36.453 --> 00:57:38.036
just slow it down.

548
00:57:38.580 --> 00:57:41.373
And buckle up for safety.

549
00:57:47.338 --> 00:57:49.548
Now, get going.

550
00:57:58.808 --> 00:58:00.517
You okay, honey?

551
00:58:00.602 --> 00:58:01.727
Mmm-hmm.

552
00:58:02.061 --> 00:58:04.271
Don't let the bedbugs bite.

553
00:58:23.750 --> 00:58:25.501
Come on. Step on it.

554
00:58:27.045 --> 00:58:29.838
Fine. We'll just
get pulled over again.

555
00:58:30.381 --> 00:58:36.553
Just shut up and drive before
I kick your fucking teeth in.

556
00:58:46.981 --> 00:58:49.525
You goddamn women drivers!

557
00:59:00.286 --> 00:59:01.787
Fuck.

558
00:59:03.456 --> 00:59:04.915
Fucking bastard.

559
00:59:22.267 --> 00:59:23.892
Shit. Andy.

560
00:59:50.295 --> 00:59:52.754
Playtime's over.

561
01:00:36.049 --> 01:00:37.799
Andy, what are
you doing?

562
01:00:37.884 --> 01:00:40.302
Come on. We've got to
get out of the building.

563
01:00:41.721 --> 01:00:44.222
Kyle, what's
going on here?

564
01:00:47.393 --> 01:00:48.894
You did this, didn't you?

565
01:00:51.898 --> 01:00:52.981
He did it.

566
01:00:55.234 --> 01:00:57.069
Get into my office.

567
01:01:01.199 --> 01:01:02.699
Is this your idea
of a joke?

568
01:01:07.413 --> 01:01:08.747
Give me that.

569
01:01:09.248 --> 01:01:10.916
Amazing, isn't it?

570
01:01:22.804 --> 01:01:23.929
Come on!

571
01:01:26.224 --> 01:01:30.560
Okay, sport, we're going to have
a little game of Chucky Says.

572
01:01:31.062 --> 01:01:33.397
Chucky says,
"Move your ass. "

573
01:01:36.651 --> 01:01:37.984
Snap out of it!

574
01:01:38.236 --> 01:01:40.821
You act like you've never seen
a dead body before.

575
01:01:48.996 --> 01:01:51.289
Andy, come on! Open it.

576
01:01:51.374 --> 01:01:53.959
Andy! Open the door!

577
01:01:54.293 --> 01:01:55.794
Come on!
Everybody out!

578
01:02:15.440 --> 01:02:17.149
Inside. Hurry.

579
01:02:41.424 --> 01:02:43.258
Stop!

580
01:02:51.058 --> 01:02:52.559
Come on.

581
01:02:52.894 --> 01:02:54.394
Come on.

582
01:02:55.062 --> 01:02:56.938
Come on.

583
01:03:08.493 --> 01:03:10.911
Hey, lady,
slow down, will you?

584
01:03:18.795 --> 01:03:20.921
* Passin' by *

585
01:03:52.745 --> 01:03:54.454
Say your prayers, Andy.

586
01:03:58.918 --> 01:04:00.085
God damn it!

587
01:04:19.605 --> 01:04:21.356
Pull over!

588
01:04:21.440 --> 01:04:22.607
What?

589
01:04:22.775 --> 01:04:23.942
Pull over!

590
01:04:24.694 --> 01:04:26.278
Pull over!

591
01:04:40.167 --> 01:04:42.127
Just what in the hell
do you think you're doing?

592
01:04:42.211 --> 01:04:43.795
Let me go. Let me go.

593
01:04:44.046 --> 01:04:46.298
What the fuck's
wrong with you?

594
01:04:48.509 --> 01:04:50.427
Let go!

595
01:04:50.678 --> 01:04:52.137
Crazy bitch!

596
01:05:50.112 --> 01:05:51.905
We're home.

597
01:05:56.077 --> 01:05:58.203
Close your eyes
and count to seven.

598
01:05:58.329 --> 01:06:00.413
When you wake,
you'll be in heaven.

599
01:06:05.962 --> 01:06:07.879
This is it, world.

600
01:06:08.005 --> 01:06:09.756
From now on,

601
01:06:09.882 --> 01:06:12.384
no more Mr. Good Guy.

602
01:06:14.720 --> 01:06:18.431
Ade due damballa.

603
01:06:19.350 --> 01:06:22.477
Give me the power,
I beg of you.

604
01:07:33.299 --> 01:07:36.468
No!

605
01:07:43.559 --> 01:07:45.310
You little shit!

606
01:07:45.561 --> 01:07:47.270
Do you know
what you've done?

607
01:07:47.563 --> 01:07:52.275
It's too late. I've spent
too much time in this body.

608
01:07:52.359 --> 01:07:54.611
I'm fucking trapped in here.

609
01:07:56.280 --> 01:07:57.739
What the hell?

610
01:07:59.408 --> 01:08:00.408
Andy, run.

611
01:08:11.962 --> 01:08:13.880
Andy.
Kyle.

612
01:08:13.964 --> 01:08:16.674
Are you okay?
Come on.

613
01:08:37.571 --> 01:08:39.197
Shit!

614
01:08:45.246 --> 01:08:47.539
Andy, hurry up.

615
01:09:09.895 --> 01:09:13.898
Let's go. I'll go first.
Stay right behind me.

616
01:09:27.454 --> 01:09:28.913
Come on.

617
01:09:38.174 --> 01:09:39.841
Andy, step on it.

618
01:09:40.134 --> 01:09:42.760
Reach! Give me your hand!

619
01:09:44.263 --> 01:09:47.557
Andy! Stop yourself.
Grab the side.

620
01:09:51.353 --> 01:09:53.938
Andy! Hurry up!
He's right behind you.

621
01:09:54.023 --> 01:09:55.523
You bastard!

622
01:10:06.368 --> 01:10:07.952
Don't look back.
Come on. Hurry!

623
01:10:11.498 --> 01:10:12.540
You can't get
away from me!

624
01:10:12.625 --> 01:10:13.625
Give me your hand!

625
01:10:14.168 --> 01:10:15.585
Reach!

626
01:10:17.254 --> 01:10:20.048
I'm going to
kill you, Andy!

627
01:10:28.474 --> 01:10:32.977
Come on. Go! Go! Go! Run down there.

628
01:10:34.647 --> 01:10:37.899
I'm going to
get you fuckers.

629
01:10:45.824 --> 01:10:47.200
God!

630
01:10:50.829 --> 01:10:53.206
Oh, God!

631
01:11:35.457 --> 01:11:37.917
Come on. Do it!

632
01:11:44.383 --> 01:11:47.218
Come on.
Give me your hand.

633
01:11:48.053 --> 01:11:49.887
Don't be afraid.
Come on.

634
01:11:52.099 --> 01:11:54.892
Closer. Closer so
you can grab my hand.

635
01:11:55.561 --> 01:11:57.854
Andy. Now!

636
01:12:09.783 --> 01:12:10.908
Can't open it.

637
01:12:11.035 --> 01:12:12.160
How will we get out?

638
01:12:12.244 --> 01:12:14.245
We'll have to find another
way. Give me your hand.

639
01:12:16.248 --> 01:12:18.583
I hate kids.

640
01:12:32.973 --> 01:12:34.932
Terrific.

641
01:15:13.425 --> 01:15:14.842
Duck!

642
01:15:27.189 --> 01:15:28.272
Do it!

643
01:15:33.111 --> 01:15:35.655
Andy, please.

644
01:15:35.781 --> 01:15:38.324
I was only playing.

645
01:15:41.954 --> 01:15:43.371
No, please!

646
01:15:55.634 --> 01:15:59.303
No! No! God! No! No! No!

647
01:16:27.040 --> 01:16:29.166
Holy shit.

648
01:16:29.918 --> 01:16:31.836
We did it.

649
01:16:36.008 --> 01:16:37.925
Let's get out of here.

650
01:16:58.614 --> 01:17:00.364
Let's see. Are you okay? Yeah.

651
01:17:00.490 --> 01:17:01.741
What's this?

652
01:17:01.867 --> 01:17:03.117
Thanks for
coming after me.

653
01:17:03.201 --> 01:17:05.745
Yeah, well, you
owe me one, squirt.

654
01:17:06.955 --> 01:17:08.205
Kyle!

655
01:17:20.135 --> 01:17:22.803
I've got you now, Andy,

656
01:17:23.388 --> 01:17:26.515
and you know what
I'm going to do to you?

657
01:17:26.600 --> 01:17:30.728
I'm going to cut off
your legs, too.

658
01:17:44.284 --> 01:17:45.284
Huh?

659
01:17:51.792 --> 01:17:53.709
No!

660
01:18:12.729 --> 01:18:14.939
Kyle! Kyle!

661
01:18:15.899 --> 01:18:18.693
Kyle! Kyle!
Kyle, wake up!

662
01:18:20.445 --> 01:18:22.113
Kyle!

663
01:18:22.823 --> 01:18:25.199
Come on. Come on.

664
01:18:46.471 --> 01:18:48.806
Ugh! God. What did
you do to him?

665
01:18:54.646 --> 01:18:56.814
All right, Andy.

666
01:19:04.656 --> 01:19:06.449
Kyle! Kyle!

667
01:19:13.498 --> 01:19:16.417
Eat this,
you son of a bitch.

668
01:19:23.341 --> 01:19:25.009
Come on.

669
01:20:12.224 --> 01:20:13.557
Where are
we going?

670
01:20:13.725 --> 01:20:15.059
Home.

671
01:20:15.685 --> 01:20:17.353
Where's home?

672
01:20:17.479 --> 01:20:20.397
Andy, I have no idea.
